# Advanced landing interactions

- Animated stat numbers always go through `<CountUp>` (`@/components/motion/count-up`) — never hand-roll
  a `useState` + `setInterval` counter.
- Reserve `<Magnetic>` (`@/components/motion/magnetic`) for the 2–3 primary CTAs/hero links per page, not
  every button — it's meant to feel special, not ambient.
- Use `<ScrollSteps>` (`@/components/motion/scroll-steps`) for a "how it works"/process section that
  reads top-to-bottom as the user scrolls through an explanation (3–6 steps). For a plain numbered grid
  with no scroll-tracked narrative, use `<Reveal stagger>` instead (see `web-ui-motion.mdc`).
- Use `<Marquee>` (`@/components/motion/marquee`) for logo strips / featured-work rows — pass it one row
  of items, it duplicates them itself. Don't build a second bespoke marquee implementation.
- Smooth/inertia page scroll (`SmoothScrollProvider`, `lenis`) is opt-in per project, not a default —
  only wire it up if the project explicitly wants an agency-site scroll feel, and never on routes with
  dense tables or long forms.
- Every effect here must no-op or simplify under `prefers-reduced-motion` — `<CountUp>` jumps straight to
  the final value, `<Marquee>` relies on Tailwind's `motion-safe:` variant, `<Magnetic>` checks
  `useReducedMotion()`. Don't remove those checks to "simplify" a component.
